 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S442-008\", \"clauses\": {\"illustrate_subtraction\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F09\", \"template\": \"{group} — There {verb} {a} {name}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F09 nests the emoji groups of F11 to F15, which print a pictorial set of objects before the count is stated, so a problem can show a set being taken away in pictures. The emoji groups are picked by the generator and are not tied to the count in a, so the pictures may not match the stated number; that is a fault recorded under F09, not a reason to mark this clause NOT_PRODUCIBLE.\"}, \"numbers_up_to_20\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F09\", \"template\": \"{group} — There {verb} {a} {name}.\", \"reasoning\": \"The printed runs for slot a in F09 are 10 to 12, 15, 20, all within 1 to 20, and the declared bound max_minuend is 20, so problems in this range are produced.\"}, \"concrete_pictorial\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F09\", \"template\": \"{group} — There {verb} {a} {name}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F09 draws its group from the emoji families F11 to F15, which are the concrete and pictorial representation the clause names.\"}, \"describe_subtraction\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F05\", \"template\": \"We are subtracting {b} from {a}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F05 is a hint that states in words what the subtraction is. Its printed values for a and b never produce a negative difference across the observed renders (F06 prints no negative result), so the sentence describes a valid subtraction.\"}, \"taking_away\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F08\", \"template\": \"Taking away {b} {name}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F08 is the question wording of taking away, which is the context the clause names. The name slot is drawn independently of the number slot, which is the agreement fault recorded under F08.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F03\", \"F04\", \"F07\", \"F08\", \"F09\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Subtract the ones: {oa} − {ob} = {od}.\", \"Subtract the tens: {ta} − {tb} = {td}.{note}\", \"How many {names} are left?\", \"Taking away {b} {name}.\", \"{group} — There {verb} {a} {name}.\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F07, F08 and F09 let the noun slot be a plural while the number slot is 1 (F08 b prints 1 in its runs) or a singular noun while the count is 10 or more, because the name slot and the number slot are independent domains with no agreement; the printed text can read as wrong grammar. F09 also draws its emoji group independently of a, with no value derivation linking them, so the stated count can disagree with the number of pictures. F04 has a note member containing the NOT_YET_KNOWN word regrouping and the 1 ten became 10 ones borrowing step, which is beyond this lc's gates. F03 derives od from ones digits with no check that the ones digit of a is at least that of b, so it can print a negative ones difference. F02, F05 and F06 were not failed: the observed results in F06 never go negative across the renders, so a is at least b in the printed domain.\"}",
